From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 39/55] cipher-switch: switch to the multithreaded cipher once
 per connection

cipher_switch() is called for every session channel the server starts. The
multithreaded AES-CTR context keeps the plain cipher name, so the test for
"ctr" in the name was true every time, and every extra session on a
multiplexed connection asked for another rekey. The sessions already running
stalled behind each one, and each rekey built a new set of cipher threads.

Remember that the switch was made in ssh->mt_enabled (set for ChaCha as well,
which the name test caught only while no multithreaded ChaCha was in use) and
return early when it is set.
---
 cipher-switch.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cipher-switch.c b/cipher-switch.c
index 26867c317..8de6bf7e2 100644
--- a/cipher-switch.c
+++ b/cipher-switch.c
@@ -47,6 +47,18 @@ cipher_switch(struct ssh *ssh) {
 	const char *recv = cipher_ctx_name(recv_cc);
 
 	debug_f("Send: %s Recv: %s", send, recv);
+
+	/*
+	 * This is called for every session channel that is started. The
+	 * switch is made once per connection: the multithreaded AES-CTR
+	 * context keeps the plain cipher name, so without this every extra
+	 * session on a multiplexed connection asked for another rekey, and
+	 * the sessions already running stalled behind each one.
+	 */
+	if (ssh->mt_enabled) {
+		debug_f("already switched");
+		return;
+	}
 	
 	/* if the name of the cipher matches then we set the context
 	 * to authenticated (it likely already is though) and then
@@ -70,6 +82,7 @@ cipher_switch(struct ssh *ssh) {
 	if ((strcmp(send, "chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com") == 0) ||
 	    (strcmp(recv, "chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com") == 0)) {
 		debug("Serial to parallel Chacha20-poly1305 cipher swap");
+		ssh->mt_enabled = 1;
 		ssh_packet_set_authenticated(ssh);
 		packet_request_rekeying();
 	}
-- 
